  "timelapse": 8,
  "steps": [
    {
      "say": "Here is an analog wristwatch! Instead of showing numbers on a screen, it tells the time with hands that sweep around a circle. Let's open it up and see how it works.",
      "do": [
        {
          "reveal": [
            "case",
            "case_back",
            "movement",
            "dial",
            "hour_hand",
            "minute_hand",
            "second_hand",
            "crystal",
            "crown",
            "strap_top",
            "strap_bottom"
          ]
        },
        {
          "zoom": "all"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "say": "On the outside, the metal case is like a tiny safe that protects everything inside. A clear crystal covers the front like a window, and two straps hold the watch on your wrist.",
      "do": [
        {
          "explode": "all"
        },
        {
          "label": [
            "case",
            "crystal",
            "strap_top",
            "strap_bottom"
          ]
        },
        {
          "highlight": [
            "case",
            "crystal"
          ]
        },
        {
          "zoom": "all"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "say": "Hidden behind the case back is the movement, the watch's engine. In many watches a small battery gives power, and a row of tiny gears turns, a bit like the gears on a bicycle passing motion along.",
      "do": [
        {
          "explode": "all"
        },
        {
          "label": [
            "movement",
            "case_back"
          ]
        },
        {
          "highlight": [
            "movement"
          ]
        },
        {
          "zoom": "movement"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "say": "All three hands sit on one little post in the middle. The thin red second hand goes all the way around in one minute. The long minute hand takes a whole hour, and the short hour hand takes twelve hours!",
      "do": [
        {
          "explode": "all"
        },
        {
          "label": [
            "second_hand",
            "minute_hand",
            "hour_hand"
          ]
        },
        {
          "highlight": [
            "second_hand",
            "minute_hand",
            "hour_hand"
          ]
        },
        {
          "spin": [
            "second_hand",
            "minute_hand",
            "hour_hand"
          ]
        },
        {
          "zoom": "dial"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "say": "The hands point to marks on the dial, the watch's face. Twelve marks stand for the twelve hours. The crown on the side is a little knob you pull and turn to set the hands to the right time.",
      "do": [
        {
          "explode": "all"
        },
        {
          "label": [
            "dial",
            "crown"
          ]
        },
        {
          "highlight": [
            "dial",
            "crown"
          ]
        },
        {
          "zoom": "crown"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "say": "Put it all back together, and the gears keep the hands turning at just the right speeds, day and night. Look at where the short and long hands point, and you can read the time!",
      "do": [
        {
          "reveal": [
            "case",
            "case_back",
            "movement",
            "dial",
            "hour_hand",
            "minute_hand",
            "second_hand",
            "crystal",
            "crown",
            "strap_top",
            "strap_bottom"
          ]
        },
        {
          "spin": [
            "second_hand",
            "minute_hand",
            "hour_hand"
          ]
        },
        {
          "zoom": "all"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "recap": "Inside a watch, tiny gears turn three hands at different speeds, so the short hand shows the hour, the long hand shows the minutes and the thin hand counts the seconds.",
  "question": "Would you like to find out how the gears make each hand turn at a different speed?",
